From 61cc3da87ed7772f39a8d122a3a017f44c2d8368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:51:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 004/147] BRING-UP: arm64: dts: qcom:
 sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2: Add a variant without dispcc

The display clock controller's probe reprograms disp_cc_pll0/1 under
the picture the UEFI left running, which blanks both panels about 22 s
into boot. Variant G is variant D with dispcc disabled, to keep that
picture while there is no display driver.

Not for upstream: a bring-up variant, built next to the main DTB.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb2.dts    | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb2.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb2.dts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..a5e2bb2a4edd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb2.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Bring-up variant G: variant D plus the display clock controller left alone.
+ * dispcc's probe reprograms disp_cc_pll0/1 under the display the UEFI left
+ * running, which blanks the panels ~22 s into boot. Not for upstream.
+ */
+#include "sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-keepfb.dts"
+
+&dispcc {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
